# Every path has a code owner, so every pull request into main needs the owner's review (or the
# owner's own bypass). Without this line, a pull request that touches no line below could be
# merged with one approval from any account with write access, and the plan bot's GitHub App
# has write access and can approve pull requests. Later lines win; they name the same owner and
# say why those paths matter most.
* @kstarev
# This file and dependabot.yml: who counts as a code owner, here and in the Plan approvals check.
/.github/ @kstarev
# Protect the access policy: every change needs a review from the code owner (AAC-007).
/access/policy/ @kstarev
/access/src/meridian_access/policy/ @kstarev
# The workflows and the plan pull request: the approvals check runs from the pull request's
# merge ref, so the ruleset (required code-owner review on these paths) is what protects it.
/.github/workflows/ @kstarev
/access/plan/ @kstarev
# The Claude budget: approving an item or moving buffer money needs the owner's review (ADR-037).
/budget/ @kstarev
